   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Peggy-O** (1 other source): Bobby played acoustic guitar on this song [4]\n- **Drums** (1 other source): Oteil played drums during this segment, and the following Space segment included Billy [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Drone**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadandcompany2021-08-27.neumann_km150.sunboy.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 194 min [1]\n- **deadandcompany2021-08-27.neumann_km150.sunboy.flac16**: source not stated; 19 songs; 194 min [2]\n- **deadco2021-08-27.SaratogaNYSPAC**: soundboard; 18 songs; 193 min [3]\n- **dac2021-08-27.AKGmix.toaste.flac16**: source not stated; 17 songs; 191 min [4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Bob Weir is listed as playing acoustic guitar at this show, alongside his rhythm guitar and vocals [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadandcompany2021-08-27.neumann_km150.sunboy.flac24**: taped by Steven Weld; transferred by Steven Weld; source: Neumann KM150's(AK50's/LC3 cables/KM100's)>GAKables xlr>Lunatec V2>GAKables xlr>Apogee Mini-Me@24/48>AES/EBU>Sound Devices 722 @24bit/48kHz ~ [1]. Also: Recorded from section 8, row EE, beside the right side of the mixer enclosure, with mics on a tall stand at 9-11 feet [1]\n- **deadandcompany2021-08-27.neumann_km150.sunboy.flac16**: taped by Steven Weld; transferred by Steven Weld; source: Neumann KM150's(AK50's/LC3 cables/KM100's)>GAKables xlr>Lunatec V2>GAKables xlr>Apogee Mini-Me@24/48>AES/EBU>Sound Devices 722 @24bit/48kHz ~ [2]\n- **deadco2021-08-27.SaratogaNYSPAC**: taped by Duncan Oldham; transferred by JT/NY; source: MK41VS>CMC6>MP6{24/48}Stand 10ft Right side of the SBD Sec 8 row gg seat 4 [3]\n- **dac2021-08-27.AKGmix.toaste.flac16**: taped by Toaste; transferred by Toaste; source: 3x AKG398 shotguns (L,C,R); 1x AKG394 Figure-8 (L,R); 2x AKG391 cardioids (L,R) > Zoom F8 @ 44.1/16 [4]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by www.bibliopolis.com: [Dead and Company - 2021 - Tour Poster - Saratoga Springs, NY - Saratoga Performing Arts Center, August 27, 2021 on Mulle](https://www.mullenbooks.com/pages/books/195308/dead-and-company-2021-tour-poster-saratoga-springs-ny-saratoga-performing-arts-center-august-27) [6]",
